{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012JHg3YNDbn6WWLncqeroSQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze this research project carefully to define three tiers for the Dream simulation.\n\nThe project is about \"exec-sim-repair-verifier\" - comparing different formulations (CLS, CWM, TRAJ) for neural code verification. The current focus is on evaluating whether adding a re-repair downstream utility section strengthens the paper enough for EMNLP 2026.\n\nKey context:\n1. The paper framing has pivoted to \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\" (empirical characterization)\n2. Core claims are about formulation equivalence at low complexity, complexity-dependent divergence, and diagnostic granularity\n\n\n3. The re-repair-phase1-instruct experiment is pending to test if CLS diagnostic information helps repair agents, but the initial phase0 control showed no meaningful difference (both around 0.82 similarity)\n4. Several DeepSeek repo-level experiments are still running across different configurations, and the paper's D116 framing already has flexibility to accommodate whatever those results show\n5. The real question is whether re-repair demonstrates meaningful gains and whether DeepSeek results cleanly support one narrative path or the other—best case would be strong re-repair improvements with decisive DeepSeek findings, median case would be moderate gains with noisier results, and worst case would be flat re-repair performance that forces us to reframe the contribution around diagnostic efficiency instead. I'm also factoring in that phase0 showed essentially no improvement using similarity metrics, but phase1 will measure actual resolve rates on Docker, which could tell a different story, and the paper already has a fallback position treating re-repair as future work if needed.\n\nNow I'm looking at the specific metrics that would determine whether this strengthens the paper—the resolve rate improvements from re-repair, how DeepSeek performs at the repo level compared to function level, and the unparseable rate differences that distinguish it from Qwen's performance.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33244,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33244},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7cf5836-3adf-4061-8b5b-792bbe0f0181","uuid":"62088fd3-d667-4764-bd4d-1a305859ab12"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012JHg3YNDbn6WWLncqeroSQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Re-repair 显著正向 + DeepSeek repo 结果清晰支持 design space characterization\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Re-repair phase1 (Docker resolve rate) 显示 CLS-diagnostic (B) 比 control (A1) 提升 10-15pp\"\n      - \"DeepSeek repo CWM unparseable rate < 20%，CWM ≈ CLS (Path B 成立: formulation advantage is model-contingent)\"\n      - \"或 DeepSeek CWM unparseable 30-50%，CLS > CWM 5-10pp (Path A: consistent advantage but smaller magnitude)\"\n      - \"Re-repair oracle (C) > CLS-diagnostic (B) > control (A1)，呈现清晰梯度\"\n    number_ranges:\n      re_repair_resolve_delta_B_vs_A1_pp: [10, 18]\n      re_repair_oracle_vs_cls_delta_pp: [5, 12]\n      deepseek_repo_cls_accuracy: [78, 85]\n      deepseek_repo_cwm_accuracy: [72, 84]\n      deepseek_repo_cwm_unparseable_pct: [5, 25]\n      deepseek_repo_cls_cwm_gap_pp: [-2, 10]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 design space characterization framing 完全成立，且新增 downstream utility section\n      作为第四贡献。Claims: (1) formulation equivalence at func-level, (2) complexity-dependent\n      divergence is model-contingent (Qwen CWM collapse vs DeepSeek CWM functional),\n      (3) diagnostic granularity at no accuracy cost, (4) diagnostic info enables\n      targeted re-repair (+10-15pp resolve rate). 论文从 empirical characterization\n      升级为 characterization + actionable downstream benefit。EMNLP Main 有力投稿。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Re-repair moderate positive 但非 decisive + DeepSeek repo 结果可解读但有噪声\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Re-repair phase1 显示 CLS-diagnostic (B) 比 control (A1) 提升 3-8pp，统计显著性边缘 (p=0.05-0.10)\"\n      - \"Oracle (C) > B 但梯度不够陡，或 Random (D) 也有部分提升（稀释 CLS-specific 贡献）\"\n      - \"DeepSeek repo CWM unparseable 15-40%，结果方向明确但 gap 较小或 seed variance 大\"\n      - \"Re-repair 在部分 prompt format 有效、部分无效（robustness check 不完全通过）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      re_repair_resolve_delta_B_vs_A1_pp: [3, 9]\n      re_repair_oracle_vs_cls_delta_pp: [2, 8]\n      deepseek_repo_cls_accuracy: [75, 82]\n      deepseek_repo_cwm_accuracy: [68, 79]\n      deepseek_repo_cwm_unparseable_pct: [15, 40]\n      deepseek_repo_cls_cwm_gap_pp: [0, 8]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Re-repair 作为 supplementary evidence 而非独立贡献。写法: \"preliminary evidence suggests\n      diagnostic granularity enables targeted re-repair (Section 6.2)\" 但不列入 core claims。\n      降低 claim 强度为 \"diagnostic information has potential downstream utility\"。\n      主线仍是三个 core claims (equivalence / divergence / granularity)。DeepSeek 结果\n      支持 design space 叙事但需要 hedge language (\"in our experimental setting\")。\n      仍投 EMNLP Main，但 accept 概率依赖 novelty perception；准备 Findings 作 realistic landing。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Re-repair flat/negative (复现 phase0 null) + DeepSeek repo 结果 confounding\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Re-repair phase1 resolve rate delta < 3pp，与 phase0 一致 (diagnostic info 不改变 repair agent 行为)\"\n      - \"或 Random (D) 与 CLS-diagnostic (B) 无显著差异（any additional context helps，非 CLS-specific）\"\n      - \"DeepSeek repo 结果出现 confound: 训练不收敛、CLS 也低于 majority baseline、或 seed variance 极大导致无法得出方向性结论\"\n      - \"No downstream utility 成为无法回应的 reviewer concern\"\n    number_ranges:\n      re_repair_resolve_delta_B_vs_A1_pp: [-2, 3]\n      re_repair_oracle_vs_cls_delta_pp: [0, 5]\n      deepseek_repo_cls_accuracy: [70, 78]\n      deepseek_repo_cwm_accuracy: [65, 78]\n      deepseek_repo_cwm_unparseable_pct: [5, 60]\n      deepseek_repo_cls_cwm_gap_pp: [-5, 5]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      完全放弃 re-repair section，不放入论文（负结果不加分反而暴露弱点）。Reframe 策略:\n      (1) 将 efficiency (6-9x speedup, 8x batch capacity) 重新定位为核心 practical contribution，\n      与 process supervision 文献对标; (2) 强化 error complementarity 分析 (oracle ensemble\n      90.63%) 作为 \"formulations are complementary, not competing\" 的证据;\n      (3) 如果 DeepSeek repo confounded，scope down 为 \"controlled study on Qwen + cross-model\n      validation at function-level with DeepSeek\"，repo-level 作为 case study 而非 systematic comparison。\n      仍投 EMNLP Main (design space characterization 本身足够)，但需确保 novelty argument\n      极其清晰: tokenizer-specific CWM failure diagnosis 是 new finding，不是 obvious。\n      若 reviewers 仍不买账，ICSE 2027 是 strong fallback (SE community 更重视 practical guidance)。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33244,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33244},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7cf5836-3adf-4061-8b5b-792bbe0f0181","uuid":"a9f1e3c2-f35f-4297-bf30-5eec5953c114"}
